  "body": "## What are you trying to do\n\nPost a nonrectangular planar punch to an Agie Classic Cut 2S. The native writer in #2951 accepts a vertical rectangular punch in the control-tested 20 mm QN2 setup.\n\n## How you imagine it working\n\nUse the nominal boundary of a single vertical prismatic punch. Preserve straight and oblique faces. Check the complete solid, the threading approach, stock clearance and the controller compensation envelope at each corner. Refuse a contour if CamCraft cannot show that the path clears the retained material. Keep the existing output for an accepted rectangle.\n\nDone means: The desktop and script can post a supported nonrectangular punch. The control plots the correct retained side on an original synthetic job. Tests cover sharp or narrow features, unsafe leads and refusal without partial output. Document the supported contours and the limits that remain.\n\nDepends on #2945.\n",
